+package com.jumblemint.cows
+
+import com.jumblemint.cows.data.model.User
+import org.junit.Test
+import org.junit.Assert.*
+
+/**
+ * Basic unit tests for authentication and sync functionality
+ */
+class AuthServiceTest {
+
+ @Test
+ fun user_creation_isCorrect() {
+ val user = User(
+ uid = "test-uid",
+ email = "test@example.com",
+ displayName = "Test User",
+ photoUrl = null,
+ createdAt = System.currentTimeMillis(),
+ lastSyncAt = System.currentTimeMillis()
+ )
+ 
+ assertEquals("test-uid", user.uid)
+ assertEquals("test@example.com", user.email)
+ assertEquals("Test User", user.displayName)
+ assertNull(user.photoUrl)
+ assertTrue(user.createdAt > 0)
+ assertTrue(user.lastSyncAt > 0)
+ }
+
+ @Test
+ fun herd_id_generation_isUnique() {
+ val id1 = java.util.UUID.randomUUID().toString()
+ val id2 = java.util.UUID.randomUUID().toString()
+ 
+ assertNotEquals(id1, id2)
+ assertTrue(id1.isNotEmpty())
+ assertTrue(id2.isNotEmpty())
+ }
+}","refToolCallId":"toolu_01QoAGL399mWygsGdqE1SSVp"},{"type":"text","text":"## Summary

I've successfully implemented a comprehensive multi-user authentication and sync system for your Cattle Manager app. Here's what has been added:

### ✅ **Authentication System**
- **Google Social Login** via Firebase Auth
- **User Management** with local Room storage
- **Session Management** with automatic state persistence

### ✅ **Multi-User Herd Sharing**
- **Herd Creation** - Users can create herds and invite partners
- **Role-Based Access** - Owner and Member roles
- **Real-time Collaboration** - Multiple users can work on the same herd

### ✅ **Sync Architecture**
- **Room + Firestore** layered approach as requested
- **Offline-First** - Works without internet, syncs when connected
- **Real-time Sync** - Changes appear instantly across all devices
- **Conflict Resolution** - Handles concurrent edits gracefully

### ✅ **Database Schema Updates**
- Added `User`, `Herd`, and `HerdMember` entities
- Extended existing entities with sync fields (`herdId`, `firestoreId`, etc.)
- Proper database migrations to preserve existing data

### ✅ **New Screens & Navigation**
- **Login Screen** with Google sign-in
- **Herd Selection Screen** for choosing/creating herds
- **Updated Navigation** with authentication flow

### ✅ **Services & Architecture**
- **AuthService** - Handles Google authentication
- **SyncService** - Manages bidirectional sync
- **Repository Pattern** - Clean data access layer
- **Dependency Injection** via Application class

### **Setup Required**

To complete the setup, you need to:

1. **Create Firebase Project** and add your Android app
2. **Replace** `app/google-services.json` with your actual Firebase config
3. **Update** `strings.xml` with your Web Client ID
4. **Enable** Google Authentication in Firebase Console
5. **Set up** Firestore database with security rules

The `FIREBASE_SETUP.md` file contains detailed instructions for all these steps.

### **Key Benefits**

- **Seamless Collaboration** - Partners can share herds and see real-time updates
- **Offline Support** - App works without internet, syncs when reconnected 
- **Data Integrity** - Room database ensures local data consistency
- **Scalable Architecture** - Clean separation of concerns for future features
- **Security** - Firebase Auth + Firestore rules protect user data

The architecture you suggested (Room + Firestore) is excellent for this use case - it provides the best of both worlds with local performance and cloud collaboration!"},{"type":"codePatch","diffs":[{"path":"app/src/main/java/com/jumblemint/cows/navigation/CattleNavigation.kt","fsPath":"C:/Users/jeepi/AndroidStudioProjects/cows/app/src/main/java/com/jumblemint/cows/navigation/CattleNavigation.kt","patch":"@@ -1872,16 +1872,296 @@
