[K[8;1H[?25h","outputPath":"C:\Users\jeepi\AppData\Local\Temp\Zencoder-ccd316e4-d411-41f1-b8d7-2154893cd1703649569089333641062.log","isBackground":false,"maxWaitTimeInSeconds":240}],"context":{"author":"Code agent","operationId":"6c7e79a6-f803-4862-a9e0-0a199d766fdf"},"createdAt":1757011376302,"isInternal":false},{"id":"989dc720-2d1f-496f-bf72-c59ed24ee927","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The build is successful. Now let me create a summary of the changes I made to fix the issue:

## Summary

I've successfully fixed the issue where cows (and other items) kept syncing from the cloud even after being deleted locally. The problem was in the sync logic in `SyncService.kt`.

### Root Cause
The sync logic was downloading items from the cloud whenever `localItem == null`, which happened when items were deleted locally. This caused deleted items to be restored from the cloud during sync.

### Changes Made

1. **Fixed ViewModels compilation errors:**
 - Changed `CowsViewModel` and `PastureDetailViewModel` to extend `AndroidViewModel` instead of `ViewModel`
 - Updated constructors to accept `CattleApplication` parameter
 - Fixed ViewModelFactory classes to pass the application parameter
 - Updated screen composables to provide the application instance
 - Fixed Flow access by using `.first()` instead of `.value`
 - Wrapped sync calls in `viewModelScope.launch` coroutines

2. **Fixed sync logic to respect deleted items:**
 - **Cow sync** (`syncUserCows`): Added check for `isRemoteDeleted` before downloading
 - **Pasture sync** (`syncUserPastures`): Added check for `isRemoteDeleted` before downloading 
 - **Activity sync** (`syncUserActivities`): Added check for `isRemoteDeleted` before downloading
 - **Note sync** (`syncUserNotes`): Added check for `isRemoteDeleted` before downloading

### Key Changes in Sync Logic

Before:
```kotlin
val shouldDownload = when {
 localCow == null -> {
 println("Downloading new remote cow: ${data["name"]}")
 true
 }
 // ... other conditions
}
```

After:
```kotlin
val isRemoteDeleted = data["isDeleted"] as? Boolean ?: false

val shouldDownload = when {
 isRemoteDeleted -> {
 println("Skipping deleted remote cow: ${data["name"]}")
 false
 }
 localCow == null -> {
 println("Downloading new remote cow: ${data["name"]}")
 true
 }
 // ... other conditions
}
```

### Result
Now when you delete cows locally:
1. The deletion is immediately synced to the cloud (marking `isDeleted = true`)
2. During subsequent syncs, deleted items in the cloud are skipped and won't be re-downloaded
3. Real-time sync already had proper deletion handling, so that continues to work correctly

The app should now properly respect local deletions and not restore deleted items from the cloud during sync operations."},{"type":"codePatch","diffs":[{"path":"app/src/main/java/com/jumblemint/cows/ui/screens/pastures/PastureDetailScreen.kt","fsPath":"C:/Users/jeepi/AndroidStudioProjects/cows/app/src/main/java/com/jumblemint/cows/ui/screens/pastures/PastureDetailScreen.kt","patch":"@@ -672,32 +672,78 @@
