-Firebase%0D%0A3. You can find the Web Client ID in your %60google-services.json%60 file or in Firebase Console %3E Project Settings %3E General tab%0D%0A%0D%0A## Step 7: Test the Setup%0D%0A%0D%0A1. Build and run the app%0D%0A2. Try to sign in with Google%0D%0A3. Check Firebase Console %3E Authentication to see if users are being created%0D%0A4. Check Firestore to see if data is being synced%0D%0A%0D%0A## Architecture Overview%0D%0A%0D%0AThe app uses a layered architecture:%0D%0A%0D%0A- **Room Database**: Local storage and offline support%0D%0A- **Firestore**: Cloud storage and real-time sync%0D%0A- **Repository Pattern**: Abstracts data sources%0D%0A- **Sync Service**: Handles bidirectional sync between Room and Firestore%0D%0A%0D%0A### Data Flow%0D%0A%0D%0A1. User actions modify local Room database immediately%0D%0A2. Sync service uploads changes to Firestore%0D%0A3. Real-time listeners detect remote changes%0D%0A4. Remote changes are merged into local database%0D%0A5. UI updates automatically via Flow/LiveData%0D%0A%0D%0A### Multi-User Support%0D%0A%0D%0A- Users authenticate with Google%0D%0A- Each user can create or join herds%0D%0A- Herds contain cattle, activities, pastures, and notes%0D%0A- Real-time sync keeps all herd members in sync%0D%0A- Offline support allows work without internet%0D%0A%0D%0A## Troubleshooting%0D%0A%0D%0A### Common Issues%0D%0A%0D%0A1. **SHA-1 Certificate Mismatch**: Make sure you've added the correct SHA-1 fingerprint%0D%0A2. **Package Name Mismatch**: Ensure Firebase project uses %60com.jumblemint.cows%60%0D%0A3. **google-services.json**: Make sure the file is in the correct location (%60app/google-services.json%60)%0D%0A4. **Internet Permission**: Ensure %60INTERNET%60 permission is in AndroidManifest.xml%0D%0A5. **Google Play Services**: Make sure Google Play Services is installed on test device%0D%0A%0D%0A### Debug Steps%0D%0A%0D%0A1. Check Android Studio logs for Firebase initialization errors%0D%0A2. Verify %60google-services.json%60 is properly configured%0D%0A3. Test authentication in Firebase Console%0D%0A4. Check Firestore rules and data structure%0D%0A5. Verify network connectivity%0D%0A%0D%0A## Security Considerations%0D%0A%0D%0A1. **Never commit** %60google-services.json%60 to public repositories%0D%0A2. Use proper Firestore security rules in production%0D%0A3. Implement proper user input validation%0D%0A4. Consider data encryption for sensitive information%0D%0A5. Regularly review Firebase security settings%0D%0A%0D%0A## Next Steps%0D%0A%0D%0A1. Implement proper error handling%0D%0A2. Add offline conflict resolution%0D%0A3. Implement user invitation system%0D%0A4. Add data export/import functionality%0D%0A5. Set up Firebase Analytics for usage tracking
+the JSON file.%0D%0A%0D%0A## Current Demo Mode%0D%0AUntil Firebase is properly configured, the app shows:%0D%0A- A warning about Firebase configuration%0D%0A- A demo button that explains what would happen%0D%0A- Debug information showing the current state%0D%0A%0D%0A## Testing%0D%0AOnce configured:%0D%0A1. The sign-in button will work normally%0D%0A2. Users can sign in with their Google accounts%0D%0A3. Data will sync across devices (when sync backend is implemented)%0D%0A4. The debug card can be removed from the SignInScreen%0D%0A%0D%0A## Note%0D%0AThe app works perfectly in local-only mode without Firebase configuration. Users can use all features with local storage.
